    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1724">

                <pb facs="1397" n="1281" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1281"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 823.124/6.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Secretary of the Treasury.</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1724-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 4, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to recent correspondence on
                    the subject of an American sanitary expert for the sanitation of Iquitos, Peru,
                    I have the honor to inform you that the Legation at Lima telegraphs under date
                    of the 3d instant that the President of Peru confides in the good <pb
                        facs="1398" n="1282" xml:id="pg1282"/> faith of any expert this Government
                    might recommend as to the duration and terms of his employment, and that he
                    authorizes the offer of a salary of seventy-five pounds sterling per month, or
                    as much as one hundred pounds. The Legation adds that if this offer should be
                    considered insufficient the President of Peru would consider a counter
                    proposal.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1724-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1724-f1-content">
                <p>Mutatis mutandis, to the Secretary of War.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
